{"name":"Still Grey","hex":"#aba9a0","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"still","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Not moving; calm.","Not effervescing; not sparkling."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Without motion.","Up to a time, as in the preceding time."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/still"},{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Back 2 You / Still Grey","blocks":[{"text":"\"Back 2 You\" / \"Still Grey\" is the third single by Australian drum and bass band Pendulum. It was released on 22 March 2004 by independent label Timeless Recordings, and was their first and only release with the label. The song \"Still Grey\" featured guest guitarist Evan Short of Concord Dawn, and was included on the CD edition of Hold Your Colour, released in July 2005."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/ca/Pendulum_-_Back_2_You_Still_Grey.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Back_2_You_%2F_Still_Grey"},{"title":"Still","blocks":[{"text":"A still is an apparatus used to distill liquid mixtures by heating to selectively boil and then cooling to condense the vapor. A still uses the same concepts as a basic distillation apparatus, but on a much larger scale. Stills have been used to produce perfume and medicine, water for injection (WFI) for pharmaceutical use, generally to separate and purify different chemicals, and to produce distilled beverages containing ethanol."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Glenfiddich_Distillery_stills.jpg/330px-Glenfiddich_Distillery_stills.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Still"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/A_still_at_Mackmyra_Whisky_Distillery.jpg/500px-A_still_at_Mackmyra_Whisky_Distillery.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/A_still_at_Mackmyra_Whisky_Distillery.jpg/1280px-A_still_at_Mackmyra_Whisky_Distillery.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/A_still_at_Mackmyra_Whisky_Distillery.jpg/500px-A_still_at_Mackmyra_Whisky_Distillery.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A still at Mackmyra Whisky Distillery","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AA_still_at_Mackmyra_Whisky_Distillery.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Coffey_Still.JPG/500px-Coffey_Still.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Coffey_Still.JPG/1280px-Coffey_Still.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Coffey_Still.JPG/500px-Coffey_Still.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Column still from Kilbeggan Distillery in County Westmeath in I